        {
          "type": "datasheet",
          "title": "Technical data",
          "note": "TEI’s technical specifications assume a 40% hydraulic power loss.",
          "tagline": "Hydraulic drilling unit for heavy excavators",
          "intro": [
            "HEMH (Hydraulic Excavator Mount “Heavy”) is the largest and most powerful of TEI’s excavator drills. Despite its size, HEMH retains the advantages of being a true attachment that does not require the excavator to be modified. The design is simple so that the equipment can be mounted and dismounted quickly.",
            "HEMH receives its hydraulic power from the excavator’s hammer circuit and requires no extra hydraulics. TEI uses in-house designed and manufactured components for consistent quality in every part of the drilling system. Our rotation and percussion systems have the powerful, lightweight design we are known for. HEMH is built to be mounted on machines of 25-30 tonnes and can be configured for most drilling methods."
          ],
